//www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/change> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ChangeLogEntry> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/change> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/timestamp> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a valid ISO-8601 dateTime\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The date and time at which the change was recorded\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"timestamp\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ChangeLogEntry> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToRemove> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Guidance on the conditions under which this tag should be removed from a UI Block\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToRemove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"whenToRemove\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToRemove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToRemove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Tag> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToRemove> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToApply> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Guidance on the conditions under which this tag should be applied to a UI Block\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToApply> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"whenToApply\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToApply> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToApply> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Tag> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/whenToApply> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/conceptType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The controlled-vocabulary type a Concept belongs to, e.g. Decision guide, Foundation, Disambiguation\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/conceptType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"conceptType\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/conceptType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/ConceptType> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/conceptType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Concept> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/conceptType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/category> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The category (facet) a Tag belongs to, e.g. documentation stage, review status, channel, implementation status\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/category> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"category\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/category> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/TagCategory> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/category> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Tag> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/category> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/gridAreas> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be valid CSS grid-area names matching the grid template\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/gridAreas> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Named CSS grid areas defined by this layout\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/gridAreas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"gridAreas\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/gridAreas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/gridAreas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Layout> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/gridAreas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Should describe the category of content the layout organises (e.g. documentation, dashboard, settings)\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/domain> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The information domain this layout is designed to navigate\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"domain\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Layout> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/domain> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/grid> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a valid CSS grid-template value or shorthand\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/grid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"CSS grid template definition for this layout\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/grid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"grid\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/grid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/grid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Layout> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/grid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasSubcomponent> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Inverse of ds:parentComponent. Each referenced entity must be a ds:Subcomponent.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasSubcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Subcomponents that are structural parts of this component\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasSubcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"hasSubcomponent\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasSubcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/parentComponent> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasSubcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/Subcomponent> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasSubcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Component> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasSubcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/parentComponent> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must reference a valid ds:Component instance\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/parentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The component to which this subcomponent structurally belongs\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/parentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"parentComponent\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/parentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/Component> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/parentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Subcomponent> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/parentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/standalone> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be true or false. When true, the subcomponent may appear in UIs without its parent.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/standalone> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Whether this subcomponent can be used independently outside its parent component\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/standalone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"standalone\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/standalone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/standalone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Subcomponent> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/standalone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/standalone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Modifiers belonging to this modifier family\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"hasModifier\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifier> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/modifierFamily> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/Modifier> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ModifierFamily> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/modifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The modifier family to which this modifier belongs\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/modifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"modifierFamily\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/modifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/ModifierFamily> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/modifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Modifier> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/modifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/modifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasVariant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The variants of this UI Block (inverse of ds:variantOf). E.g. Tooltip has variant Tooltip+Dense.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasVariant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"hasVariant\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasVariant> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/variantOf> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasVariant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasVariant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasVariant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/variantOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The base UI Block this block is a variant of, by the '+' naming convention (e.g. Tooltip+Dense is a variant of Tooltip). Distinct from ds:inheritsFrom: a variant is a modifier-style derivative rather than a prefixed specialisation.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/variantOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"variantOf\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/variantOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/hasVariant> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/variantOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/variantOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/variantOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/specializedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The UI Blocks that inherit from / specialise this block (inverse of ds:inheritsFrom). E.g. Tooltip is specialised by DataTooltip.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/specializedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"specializedBy\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/specializedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/inheritsFrom> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/specializedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/specializedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/specializedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/inheritsFrom> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must reference a valid ds:UIBlock that this block specialises, and must follow the rules of inheritance (to be specified in full later). One such rule: the inheriting block's name is the parent block's name with a prefix applied (e.g. Tooltip -> DataTooltip, Button -> DropdownButton). Should not be cyclic.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/inheritsFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The UI Block this block inherits from / specialises (e.g. a Data tooltip inherits from Tooltip). Distinct from subcomponent containment: inheritance is an is-a-specialisation relationship.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/inheritsFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"inheritsFrom\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/inheritsFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/specializedBy> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/inheritsFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/inheritsFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/inheritsFrom> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/changeLog> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Links a UI Block to its dated change log entries.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/changeLog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"changeLog\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/changeLog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/ChangeLogEntry> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/changeLog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/changeLog> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentationStage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Links a UI Block to the documentation-stage Tag(s) applied to it (e.g. needs:documentation). One facet of the wider Tag vocabulary; the other tag facets are tracked as future work.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentationStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"documentationStage\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentationStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/Tag> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentationStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentationStage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Links a UI Block to its configurable properties\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"hasProperty\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/Property> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasProperty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Links a UI Block to applicable modifier families\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"hasModifierFamily\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/ModifierFamily> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasModifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/knownEdgeCases> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Free-text notes on edge cases, caveats, or open questions for the Concept.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/knownEdgeCases> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"known edge cases\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/knownEdgeCases> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/knownEdgeCases> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Concept> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/knownEdgeCases> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/content> <https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance> \"Write the concept as a complete Markdown document: open with what it is and why it matters, then cover the guidance in structured sections with concrete, real-world examples.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/content> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Should be a self-contained Markdown document that fully explains the concept, with clear sections and concrete examples. May reference UIBlocks and other concepts by name or link.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/content> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The long-form Markdown body of a Concept — the full documentation text (sections, prose, tables, links). Stored as a plain string literal; the content is Markdown.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/content> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"content\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/content> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/content> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Concept> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/content> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> <https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance> \"Provide detailed guidelines for correctly using and implementing the UI block. Include best practices for accessibility, responsiveness, content handling, localization, animation, and keyboard interaction. Ensure that the guidelines are comprehensive and cover all important aspects of using and implementing the component correctly.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"These guidelines should contain the best practices for accessibility, responsiveness, content handling, localization, animation and keyboard interaction of this UI block. They should be comprehensive and cover all important aspects of using and implementing the component correctly.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Detailed specification for correctly using and implementing the UI block.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"guidelines\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/guidelines> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/usage> <https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance> \"Document when and when not to use the component, with a short general description. Cover all use cases and anti-patterns distinctly, name the alternative component for discouraged uses, and draw examples from real released usage.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/usage> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Should include a general description and clear When-to-use / When-not-to-use guidance. Each scenario should be distinct; when discouraging a use, name the component to use instead. All variants should be considered. Examples should be drawn from real-world, released usage.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/usage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Free-text (Markdown) usage documentation for the UI block. Subsumes the former whenToUse/whenNotToUse: a usage entry describes the contexts where the component is most appropriate ('When to use'), the contexts where it is NOT appropriate and what to use instead ('When not to use'), and a general description, typically as Markdown sub-sections.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/usage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"usage\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/usage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/usage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/usage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be valid YAML conforming to the Anatomy DSL specification. Root node must be named (have uri). See skills/anatomy-author/SKILL.md for format.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"YAML specification of component structure using the Anatomy DSL. Describes nodes (named/anonymous), edges with cardinality, slots, and CTI-inspired styles.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"anatomyDsl\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyDsl> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Identifies all significant UI block parts and their relationships. Parts are decomposed only to the level where they are meaningful and reusable (e.g., if a component is made of other published components, reference those components instead of redescribing them). Each part is assigned a descriptive name, visual slot and description of its role in the overall component structure. Relationships between parts are documented: cardinality (1, 0..1, 1..*) and nesting (which parts are contained within others). Includes visual annotations or diagrams showing the anatomical structure. Both visual representation and text list align and describe the same parts. No orphaned or unnamed parts—every element in the anatomy is accounted for\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"DEPRECATED. Legacy anatomy field (free-form text). Superseded by ds:anatomyDsl.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"anatomyClassic\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/anatomyClassic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/figmaLink> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a valid URL pointing to the Figma design file for this UI block. The URL should be accessible and correctly formatted.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/figmaLink> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Link to the Figma design file for this UI block\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/figmaLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"figmaLink\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/figmaLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/figmaLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/figmaLink> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance> \"Assign the UI block to a specific tier within the design system. Choose from predefined tier values such as core, global, global_form, apps, site, etc. This property is mandatory and should have only one value.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Has to be mandatory and singular. Must be one of the predefined tier values (core, global, global_form, apps, site, etc.).\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The tier to which the UI block belongs to\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"tier\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/Tier> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/tier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/decisionLog> <https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance> \"Document any decisions made regarding the entity, including the date of the decision, the author responsible for the decision, and a clear explanation of the change or decision made. This log helps maintain a history of changes and the rationale behind them.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/decisionLog> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"[date] Contains the date of the decision made, [author] Links to the decision maker, [content] Contains the reasons of change, is clear on what the change is\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/decisionLog> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Log of decisions with [date][author][content]\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/decisionLog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"decisionLog\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/decisionLog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/decisionLog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/decisionLog> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/version> <https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance> \"Provide a semantic version number following the MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH format (e.g., 1.0.0, 2.1.3). Include optional pre-release identifiers (e.g., 1.0.0-alpha) and build metadata (e.g., 1.0.0+build.123456789).\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/version> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must follow semantic versioning format: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH with optional pre-release and build metadata\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/version> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Semantic version of the entity following semver specification\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/version> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"version\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/version> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/SemverString> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/version> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/version> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/version> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/summary> <https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance> \"Write an introduction that gives a quick overview of the entity. Start with the primary purpose and list all the main use cases. Make sure to include information that can help users decide if this is the right element they need.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/summary> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Concise paragraph (3-5 sentences) that clearly describes the purpose of the entity, lists at least 2-3 use cases, and is written in a clear and accessible way. Enables readers to quickly determine if this is the right component for their needs.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/summary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A comprehensive paragraph of text that states the singular purpose of the entity.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/summary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"summary\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/summary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/summary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/summary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/name> <https://ds.canonical.com/completionGuidance> \"Provide a clear and descriptive name for the entity that accurately reflects its purpose and functionality within the design system.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/name> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a concise, descriptive name that clearly identifies the entity. Should be unique within the design system and avoid generic terms like 'button' or 'input' without context.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/name> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A human-readable text for the entity. The primary identifier, used for referencing and display purposes.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"name\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/name> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ConceptType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A controlled-vocabulary classification of a Concept (e.g. 'Decision guide', 'Foundation', 'Disambiguation').\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ConceptType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Concept Type\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ConceptType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ConceptType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Concept> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A standalone piece of design-system documentation not bound to a single UIBlock — a cross-cutting guide, disambiguation, foundation, or decision (e.g. 'Foundations: Grid', 'Disambiguation: Badge/Chip/Tag'). Carries a long-form Markdown body (content), an optional short summary, a concept type, and a tier.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Concept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Concept\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Concept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Concept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ChangeLogEntry> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A single dated record of a change to a UIBlock, with a timestamp, the change description, an owner, an optional GitHub link, and a change type.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ChangeLogEntry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Change Log Entry\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ChangeLogEntry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ChangeLogEntry> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/TagCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A facet that groups related Tags (e.g. 'documentation stage', 'review status', 'channel', 'implementation status').\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/TagCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Tag Category\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/TagCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/TagCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Tag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A controlled-vocabulary label applied to a UIBlock. Tags are grouped into facets by their category (e.g. 'documentation stage', 'review status', 'channel', 'implementation status'). The category-typed views over this vocabulary are tracked as future work; for now a Tag carries its name, category, and apply/remove guidance.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Tag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Tag\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Tag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Tag> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A code library or package that provides platform-specific implementations of UIBlocks\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Implementation Library\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Platform-specific implementation of a UI Block\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Implementation Object\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Tier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A scope level in the design system hierarchy that determines where UIBlocks are intended to be used (e.g. global, apps, site)\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Tier\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Tier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Property> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A configurable property of a UI Block\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Property> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Property\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Property> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Property> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ModifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A grouping of related modifiers that can be applied to UI Blocks\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ModifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Modifier Family\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ModifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIElement> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/ModifierFamily> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Modifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A named variant value within a ModifierFamily that alters the appearance or behaviour of a UIBlock (e.g. 'primary', 'secondary' within the 'importance' family)\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Modifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Modifier\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Modifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIElement> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Modifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Group> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A collection UIBlock: a container that arranges multiple instances of a single sibling UIBlock (typically a Component) as a repeating series. The plural counterpart of a singular Component (e.g. Cards groups Card units, Tiles groups Tile units), responsible for their shared layout rather than for any content of its own.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Group\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Group> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Subcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A named part of a Component that has design-system identity but is typically not used independently outside its parent\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Subcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Subcomponent\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Subcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Subcomponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Layout> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Layouts are an opinionated division of space to navigate a domain of information.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Layout> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Layout\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Layout> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Layout> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Pattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A reusable solution to a recurring user problem in a specific context\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Pattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Pattern\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Pattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Pattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Component> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"An implementable piece of user interface defined by its appearance and behaviour\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Component> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Component\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Component> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Component> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A category of visual or abstract entity that fulfills a particular role in composing user interfaces\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"UI Block\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIElement> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/UIElement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Base class for all visual and interactive design system elements\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/UIElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"UI Element\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/UIElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/UIElement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/Entity> <http://www.w3.org